.TH tkutab n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutab
.PP
A tabbed container with the conveniences a file manager needs that a bare \fBttk::notebook\fR lacks: a "+" new\-tab button and closeable tabs (middle\-click, or a close call from the caller). Each tab is a frame the caller fills with its own content. Tk 8.6+ and 9.x.
.SS API
.CS
::tkutils::tkutab::widget   path ?options?
::tkutils::tkutab::add      path label      ;# add a tab, returns its content frame
::tkutils::tkutab::close    path frame      ;# close the tab holding frame
::tkutils::tkutab::current  path            ;# content frame of the active tab
::tkutils::tkutab::setLabel path frame label
::tkutils::tkutab::tabs     path            ;# list of content frames, in order
::tkutils::tkutab::count    path            ;# number of open tabs
.CE
.SS Options
.IP \(bu
\fB\-onnew\fR    script \-\- run when the "+" button is pressed (typically calls \fBadd\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-onclose\fR  script, appended the closing frame \-\- run when a tab is closed.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-onselect\fR script, appended the selected frame \-\- run when the active tab changes.
.SS Use
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutab

::tkutils::tkutab::widget .tabs \
    -onnew    {apply {{} {newTab}}} \
    -onselect {apply {f {puts "now on $f"}}}
pack .tabs -fill both -expand 1

proc newTab {} {
    set f [::tkutils::tkutab::add .tabs "untitled"]
    # fill $f with this tab's content
    ttk::label $f.l -text "content of [::tkutils::tkutab::count .tabs]"
    pack $f.l
}
newTab
.CE
.PP
\fBadd\fR returns the content frame; put the tab's widgets inside it. \fBcurrent\fR gives the active tab's frame, so per\-tab state can be keyed by frame path. A tab is closed with middle\-click or by calling \fBclose\fR; \fB\-onclose\fR fires so the caller can release that tab's resources.
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtkufilelist\fR, \fBtkufiletree\fR, \fBtkupath\fR
